From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iphlpapi: GetPerAdapterInfo lists the adapter's own name servers (9462)

GetPerAdapterInfo gave every adapter the system's name servers (DnsQueryConfig with no adapter), while GetAdaptersAddresses and ipconfig already list each adapter's own (9210: the fixed NameServer, else the lease's DhcpNameServer of Tcpip\Parameters\Interfaces\{GUID}). Windows' GetPerAdapterInfo lists the adapter's IPv4 servers -- a DHCP adapter its lease's, a released one none. get_dns_server_list now asks DnsQueryConfig(DnsConfigDnsServerList) for the adapter by its GUID name, as GetAdaptersAddresses does; GetNetworkParams (no adapter) keeps the system's list. This was held back in 9210 because Wine Mono's IPv4InterfaceProperties passed a fixed one-server structure whatever size it was told and an adapter with two or more servers overran it; Wine Mono sg37 (sg-image mono-0035) allocates the size asked for, as the .NET Framework does (ledger i0690). The same overrun hit sg36 already on a machine whose resolv.conf lists two or more servers.

Gate: test-tcpipreg section 8 (GetPerAdapterInfo per adapter, released adapter none; .NET GetIPv4Properties 200 rounds with SG_MONO_DIR = sg37). Mutant SG_MUTANT_PERADAPTER_SYSTEM_SERVERS.
---
--- a/dlls/iphlpapi/iphlpapi_main.c
+++ b/dlls/iphlpapi/iphlpapi_main.c
@@ -2862,12 +2862,24 @@
     IP4_ARRAY *servers = (IP4_ARRAY *)buf;
     DWORD needed, num, err, i, array_len = sizeof(buf);
     IP_ADDR_STRING *ptr;
+    WCHAR name[CHARS_IN_GUID];
+    const WCHAR *adapter = NULL;
+    GUID guid;
 
     if (luid && luid->Info.IfType == MIB_IF_TYPE_LOOPBACK) return ERROR_NO_DATA;
 
+    /* Stained Glass OS (i0690): an adapter's own name servers (DnsQueryConfig by its GUID name,
+     * as GetAdaptersAddresses asks, 9210), not the system's, as Windows' GetPerAdapterInfo lists
+     * them; GetNetworkParams (no adapter) keeps the system's */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PERADAPTER_SYSTEM_SERVERS
+    if (luid && !ConvertInterfaceLuidToGuid( luid, &guid ) &&
+        !ConvertGuidToStringW( &guid, name, ARRAY_SIZE(name) ))
+        adapter = name;
+#endif
+
     for (;;)
     {
-        err = DnsQueryConfig( DnsConfigDnsServerList, 0, NULL, NULL, servers, &array_len );
+        err = DnsQueryConfig( DnsConfigDnsServerList, 0, adapter, NULL, servers, &array_len );
         if (err != ERROR_SUCCESS && err != ERROR_MORE_DATA) goto err;
         num = (array_len - FIELD_OFFSET(IP4_ARRAY, AddrArray[0])) / sizeof(IP4_ADDRESS);
         needed = num * sizeof(IP_ADDR_STRING);
